{"book":5,"chapter":23,"context":{"chapter":23,"title":"Who May Enter the Assembly","summary":"Rules define who may join the assembly of the Lord, how to keep the war camp clean, and how to treat runaway slaves, loans, vows and a neighbor's crops.","background":"Ammonites and Moabites were excluded because they withheld bread and water and hired Balaam to curse Israel (vv. 3–4); readers have long noticed the tension with Ruth, a Moabite who became David's great-grandmother. Protecting a runaway slave (vv. 15–16) was unusual: other ancient codes, such as Hammurabi's, punished those who sheltered runaways.","customs":[{"term":"Paddle upon thy weapon","verses":"23:12-14","note":"Soldiers relieved themselves outside the camp and buried the waste with a digging tool, 'for the Lord thy God walketh in the midst of thy camp.'"},{"term":"Plucking grain","verses":"23:25","note":"A hungry traveler could pick grain by hand from a neighbor's field, but not use a sickle. Jesus' disciples did this in Mark 2:23."}],"watchFor":["Each nation's treatment is tied to its history with Israel (vv. 3–8).","No interest on loans to a fellow Israelite; KJV 'usury' simply means interest (vv. 19–20).","Vows are optional, but once made must be kept (vv. 21–23)."],"connections":["Numbers 22:5-6","Nehemiah 13:1-3","Ecclesiastes 5:4-5","Mark 2:23-24"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["לֹא","lo'-","H3808","HTn","not"],["יָבֹא","yavo'","H935","HVqi3ms","he will go"],["פְצוּעַ","fetzua'-","H6481","HVqsmsc","[one who] is wounded of"],["דַּכָּא","daka'","H1795","HNcfsa","crushing"],["וּכְרוּת","ukherut","H3772","HC/Vqsmsc","and [one who] is cut off of"],["שָׁפְכָה","shafekhah","H8212","HNcfsa","penis"],["בִּקְהַל","bikhal","H6951","HR/Ncmsc","in [the] assembly of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"]],"x":[[48003028,48003028,6],[23056003,23056004,5],[3021017,3021021,4],[5023002,5023003,4],[16013001,16013003,4],[3022022,3022024,3],[5023008,5023008,3],[25001010,25001010,3]],"xn":8},"2":{"w":[["לֹא","lo'-","H